 ] [
 .B ce_threshold
-TIME ]
+TIME ] [
+.B pp
+]
 
 .SH DESCRIPTION
 CoDel (pronounced "coddle") is an adaptive "no-knobs" active queue management
@@ -60,6 +62,9 @@ packets are no longer dropped.
 
 Additional details can be found in the paper cited below.
 
+CoDel++ modifies CoDel's control law to better adapt to high-speed congestion
+control algorithms, improving queue delay and throughput trade-off.
+
 .SH PARAMETERS
 .SS limit
 is the hard limit on the real queue size. When this limit is reached, incoming packets
@@ -92,6 +97,10 @@ sets a threshold above which all packets are marked with ECN Congestion
 Experienced. This is useful for DCTCP-style congestion control algorithms that
 require marking at very shallow queueing thresholds.
 
+.SS pp
+can be used to enable CoDel++ (pp stands for ++). By default,
+.B pp
+is disabled.
 
 .SH EXAMPLES
  # tc qdisc add dev eth0 root codel
@@ -112,6 +121,14 @@ interval 30.0ms ecn
      count 0 lastcount 0 ldelay 76us drop_next 0us
      maxpacket 2962 ecn_mark 0 drop_overlimit 0
 
+ # tc qdisc add dev eth0 root codel pp
+ # tc -s qdisc show
+   qdisc codel 8008: dev eth0 root refcnt 2 limit 1000p target 5ms
+interval 100ms pp
+    Sent 40520 bytes 57 pkt (dropped 0, overlimits 0 requeues 0)
+    backlog 0b 0p requeues
+     count 0 lastcount 0 ldelay 0us drop_next 0us
+     maxpacket 0 ecn_mark 0 drop_overlimit 0
 
 .SH SEE ALSO
 .BR tc (8),
